# UniFi Connect APK versioning

UniFi Connect rejects APK uploads with "Outdated App File" unless `versionCode` is **strictly higher** than the installed app.

## When building or handing over an APK

- After any change meant for the UniFi Display, run `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` (or `assembleRelease` / `packageDebug` / `packageRelease`). Those tasks auto-bump `versionCode` and `versionName` in `app/version.properties`.
- Never tell the user to upload an existing `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` without rebuilding first.
- Never reuse a previously built APK. Rebuild even if sources look unchanged — a second assemble produces a higher `versionCode`.
- Do not bump by hand-editing `defaultConfig` in `app/build.gradle.kts`. Do not bump on Gradle sync or compile-only tasks.
- Do not auto-commit `app/version.properties` (a dirty tree after assemble is expected).

```bash
# ❌ BAD — reuse last APK
# "Upload app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk"

# ✅ GOOD — rebuild so versionCode increases
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
# then upload app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
```
